{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.452,
   "text": "Every Thanksgiving, Dad drove us home through the mountains. And every year, the same warning."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.052,
   "end": 15.599,
   "text": "After the tunnel, never look in the rearview mirror. And if you do... don't let her see you look."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.499,
   "end": 18.909,
   "text": "He never said who she was."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 19.909,
   "end": 25.584,
   "text": "This year, Dad was too tired, so I drove. He was asleep before we reached the tunnel."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.284,
   "end": 30.529,
   "text": "When we came out the other side, I checked the mirror. Just habit."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 31.529,
   "end": 34.239,
   "text": "There was a woman in the back seat."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 35.639,
   "end": 41.655,
   "text": "Gray coat. Soaking wet. Long black hair hanging over her face... staring down at the floor."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 42.455,
   "end": 47.724,
   "text": "I snapped my eyes back to the road. I drove twenty miles without breathing."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 48.424,
   "end": 52.264,
   "text": "Behind me, I could hear water... dripping onto the seat."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.264,
   "end": 59.043,
   "text": "At the first gas station, I shook Dad awake and told him everything."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.743,
   "end": 62.452,
   "text": "He went pale. Did she see you look?"
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.652,
   "end": 66.425,
   "text": "No, I said. She never looked up."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 67.425,
   "end": 71.564,
   "text": "Dad closed his eyes... and let out a long, slow breath."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 72.964,
   "end": 76.164,
   "text": "Then I glanced at the mirror one last time."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start": 77.764,
   "end": 82.585,
   "text": "Her head was up now. And through all that wet hair... she was smiling at me."
  }
 ],
